  "model": "s2.1-pro-free",
  "text": "I'm glad you shared it with us. I've been writing about the evenings I spent waiting here. I'd like you to hear my story.\n\nAfter the last boat returns, then. That gives Mara time to finish. Let’s make sure she and Sol know when we’ll be here.\n\n“I thought she had nothing more she wanted to tell us. I should have asked her. Come and sit where we can read it.”\n\nMara held out her plate for another slice. I cut her a piece before the wind could suggest any more improvements.\n\nThe seed stays dark in a boat or a hand. Its lantern-flower grows only after its roots reach the garden’s soil.\n\nYes. That gives Mara time to finish work. We still need to agree who will read and tell our friends the plan.\n\nWe kept our promise. I like knowing that flower began with the two of us. What did you find on your way here?\n\nThere you are! I’ve been looking toward the river. Come and plant the seed with me while it’s still light.\n\n“Next time, I’ll bring a heavier tablecloth,” I said. Sol considered this while he finished his slice.\n\nAll that happened before the storm took the footbridge. By then, the garden had already grown quiet.\n\nShe came all the way to your workshop with the loaf. I’m glad you kept that part in the story.\n\n“We’ll need to secure the corners,” he said. “Unless you want us to eat standing like this.”\n\nI wanted to hear from you. I didn’t know you were waiting for a different sort of story.\n\nOne corner had folded under. I pulled it straight, then sat down with my story.\n\n“Next time, we’ll plant it together. There’s a place for it beside the others.”\n\nYou helped arrange today's gathering, Pip. Would you like to welcome everyone?\n\nI’m glad you could stay for my story, Mara. I’ve missed having you beside me.",
